<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  airkg-dispatch — launchd job for the standing dispatcher.
  Task: cc_tasks/2026-09-15_standing_dispatcher.md §2, decision 7.
  Design: docs/design/2026-09-15_DN-006_standing_dispatcher.md decision 1.

  launchd IS the loop; `seldon dispatch once` is the pass. There is no daemon to supervise.

  StartInterval is seldon.yaml `dispatch.poll_interval_s` (300 s) and has NO MEASURED BASIS —
  see the comment on that key. The two must be changed together; the wrapper refuses if they
  disagree, so the plist cannot drift away from the file that explains it.

  RunAtLoad is false: loading the job should not fire a pass, because a pass can launch a CC
  session and `launchctl load` is something an operator does while looking at something else.

  Installed by SYMLINK, never a copy (operator doctrine; and the reason is this file):
    ln -s /Users/brock/GitHub/ai-readiness-kg/scripts/jobs/com.brock.airkg-dispatch.plist \
          ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.brock.airkg-dispatch.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.brock.airkg-dispatch.plist
  A copy would be a second StartInterval to keep in step with this one and with seldon.yaml's
  poll_interval_s — three files holding one parameter, and the wrapper's drift check can only
  see two of them. The symlink makes the installed job and the tracked file the same bytes.

  Installed and loaded by `cc_tasks/2026-09-16_cadence_and_enable.md` §3, which is also the
  task that set `dispatch.enabled: true`. Before it, a loaded job was a no-op that said
  `dispatch is disabled` and wrote nothing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.brock.airkg-dispatch</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/brock/GitHub/ai-readiness-kg/scripts/jobs/airkg_dispatch.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/brock/GitHub/ai-readiness-kg</string>
</dict>
</plist>
